import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Caring for linen — AASRA Journal" description="Wash cool, line-dry, never fear the crease — living with pure linen.">
  <div class="page-title-block">
    <div class="kicker">Journal · Care</div>
    <h1>Caring for linen</h1>
    <p class="page-sub">A short guide to living with pure linen.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;">
      <img src="/images/products/linen-curtain-ivory-2.webp" alt="Folded ivory linen" loading="eager" width="1600" height="1000" style="width:100%; aspect-ratio:16/10; object-fit:cover; display:block; margin-bottom:2.5rem;" />

      <div class="prose">
        <p>The first thing to know about pure linen is that the crease is not a flaw. It is the fabric breathing — a record of the curtain you pulled back this morning, the cushion someone leaned against. Cotton-linen blends exist to suppress it. We do not sell blends.</p>
        <p>Wash linen cool, at 30°C, with a mild detergent, and skip the bleach entirely — it eats the flax fibre's natural sheen. Tumble-dry on low only if you must; line-drying in shade keeps the drape alive. Iron it damp if you want a smooth finish, or smooth it with your hands and let it dry as it hangs.</p>
        <p>Stains want speed, not force: blot, never rub, with cold water first. For curtains, an annual wash is plenty — vacuum the fullness monthly with the brush head instead. For cushions, wash the covers inside-out and let the panels relax a day before restuffing.</p>
        <p>And whatever you do, do not fear the softening. Linen is one of the few textiles that gets better with washing — the fibre relaxing, the drape deepening, the surface growing supple. The panel you buy is the roughest it will ever be.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="service-links" style="justify-content:flex-start; margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <a href="/shop?category=home-textiles">Shop the linens</a>
        <a href="/journal">Back to the Journal</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 2; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .prose p:first-of-type { color: var(--text); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.7; }
</style>
